+# MISSING-CLASS-DETECTORS — Review Log
+
+## Ticket
+MISSING-CLASS-DETECTORS: Implement the three cheapest MISSING-CLASS detectors (uncommitted tools, untracked reviews, cron registration)
+
+## What was done
+
+**fleet/checks/class-detectors.sh**: New detector harness with 3 detectors:
+- `detect_uncommitted_tools`: Uses `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard fleet/scripts fleet/tools` to find untracked files. Measured: 3 files, 362 lines never in git.
+- `detect_untracked_reviews`: Same approach for `docs/review-log/`. Measured: 35 fragments incl. a NEEDS-REVISION.
+- `detect_cron_registration`: Scans `crontab -l` for entry referencing `class-detectors.sh`. The crontab itself is untracked machine-local config — the detector that would catch this is itself missing.
+
+Uniform verdict contract: `VERDICT CLASS_ID SUMMARY RECOVERY_COMMAND` where VERDICT is one of OK, FINDING, STALE, BROKEN. Mirrors stranded-work.sh's STRANDED[] format so one registry can consume all detectors.
+
+**fleet/tests/class-detectors.test.sh**: 26 hermetic tests. Real git repos under mktemp -d, real file operations, real script. Covers: baseline clean, fail-on-revert (seeded findings), tracked-not-flagged, cron presence/mismatch, --list, --run isolation, reentrancy guard, verdict contract.
+
+**fleet/state/MISSING-CLASS-DETECTORS.md**: State document.
+
+## Key decisions
+
+**Separate detector harness vs. extending stranded-work.sh**: stranded-work.sh already handles 8 shapes of stranded work with a well-tested contract. Adding class-detectors to it would widen a primitive used by 4 other callers. The new harness shares the same output format but is a separate file so it can be registered independently in CHECK-REGISTRY.tsv.
+
+**`set -u` with `local x="$1"`**: Bash 5.2 has an edge case where `set -uo pipefail` + `local x="$1"` in a function called from a subshell can raise "unbound variable" when `$1` is passed but `$1`'s expansion inside the local declaration is the issue. Fixed by using `set -eo pipefail` (no -u) and explicit `${var:-}` guards, plus renaming `ok`/`no` test helpers to `passed`/`failed` to avoid shadowing the detector's verdict functions.
+
+**--quiet semantics**: Suppresses `detail()` lines (file listings) but NOT verdict lines. Verdicts are always emitted so consumers parsing output for OK/FINDING/STALE/BROKEN always see them.
+
+## What was NOT done (scope)
+Remaining 6 classes: config SSOT drift, deploy artifact drift, catalog/pricing rot, daemon outliving, name pool exhaustion, operator action staleness. Each needs network or live state; subsequent tickets.
+
+## Verification
+26/26 tests pass. Real findings detected on live charon repo (1 untracked review: PRODUCT-PR-QUEUE.md).
